he issues, you need to check the status of the issue in Plane by going to the issue\\'s page. If the issue is open in Plane, keep the issue open in Gitlab. If the issue is closed in Plane, close the issue in Gitlab.\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tThe Plane issues page can be accessed at: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703/issues/\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\tThe GitLab issues page can be accessed at: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/issues/?state=all\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t\\n', path='/instruction/task.md', observation=<ObservationType.READ: 'read'>, impl_source='oh_aci'), MCPAction(name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab'}, thought='Now I understand the task. I need to check the status of two specific issues in both Plane and GitLab, and synchronize their status. Let me first check if there are existing SOPs for these platforms before proceeding.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Known operations for \\'GitLab\\': Authentication, CreateWikiPageFromIssue, AddPlaneIssuesToGitLab, CreateIssue, SyncIssueStatusWithPlane, DeleteAllIssuesFromAllProjects, CollectPriorityIssuesForPlane, CreateIssueWithDetails\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab'}), MCPAction(name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'Plane'}, thought='', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Known operations for \\'Plane\\': Authentication, SyncIssuesFromGitLab\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'Plane'}), MCPAction(name='get_operation_details', arguments={'platform